{"availability":"available","full":"uehaj/sys1grep","name":"sys1grep","description":"grep by meaning, across languages. TypeSafe Jev scores every line against a meaning; combine meanings with AND/OR/NOT. 意味で探す grep。日本語で英語を、英語で日本語を検索できる","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":148,"forks":9,"created":"2026-09-19T03:18:28Z","updated":"2026-10-06T13:16:14Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://uehaj.github.io/sys1grep/","topics":[],"demo":"https://sys1grep.js.org/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:50.355Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:50.355Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:50.355Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:50.355Z","stars":148,"forks":9}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Background and design notes (Japanese): Jevのキラーアプリ、「意味で探す grep」を作った on Zenn.","Renamed from semgrep (0.5.0). Two reasons. The name collided with the static-analysis tool Semgrep, a trademark. And the tool was never meant for Jev alone: it targets System 1 models in general, and I'd like it to work with any models TypeSafe AI may release after Jev under other names :). So from 0.5.0 this is sys1grep (System 1 + grep): npm package @uehaj/sys1grep (was @uehaj/semgrep), commands sys1grep / git sys1grep, environment SYS1GREP, config /.config/sys1grep/.env. The old SEMGREP names and /.config/semgrep/.env still work for one minor release, each use printing a deprecation line;…","A grep that finds lines by what they mean, not by regular expressions. Matching is done by Jev, the System One model from TypeSafe AI. Jev does not generate text. It answers typed questions with probabilities, so for every line sys1grep asks \"does this line match the meaning network failure?\", gets a probability back, and applies a threshold."],"features":["Zero dependencies. One file, Node.js 20.16+ and fetch.","Fast. 30 lines go into one request, requests run 8 at a time. A 210-line file finishes in under a second.","Meanings combine with AND / OR / NOT.","Language-agnostic. The meaning and the text can each be in any language. A Japanese meaning finds French, Russian, Chinese and Korean lines alike. No translation step, same speed, same cost."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/uehaj/sys1grep/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1dfbbe1c69b69049b75ee59e33a7df00d0aca01d82086e525550da81c08c539a","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:50.523Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:50.523Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Background and design notes (Japanese): Jevのキラーアプリ、「意味で探す grep」を作った on Zenn.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/uehaj/sys1grep/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"The question costs one small request per meaning, sent only when -r / git sys1grep found something to","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/uehaj/sys1grep/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Every route needs it, the page itself included: without it (in the query, or in a header for the page's own requests) the server answers 404 to everything, so another local account or process cannot read the page, its token, or a search's results merely by knowing the port.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/uehaj/sys1grep/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"A --sys1-api-key inside opts, and a url's userinfo, come back masked as , the same way --verbose masks them; opts refuses a target, a flag the page itself refuses at launch, or --sys1-url / --sys1-api-key (their own fields), and url and a URL summarizer must be http(s).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/uehaj/sys1grep/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"1dfbbe1c69b69049b75ee59e33a7df00d0aca01d82086e525550da81c08c539a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/uehaj/sys1grep/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:50.524Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-06T13:16:14Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl